      <p>The tabs are Errors, Project Validation, Terminal, and Inspector.</p>
      <h3 id="errors" class="group scroll-mt-20">Errors<a href="#errors" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h3>
      <p>Validation results for the document in front. Selecting an entry jumps to the place it refers to.</p>
      <h3 id="project-validation" class="group scroll-mt-20">Project Validation<a href="#project-validation" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h3>
      <p>Results from a project-wide run, such as <strong>Project &gt; Validate &gt; Project</strong>, and output from long-running operations including DITA-OT builds.</p>
      <h3 id="inspector" class="group scroll-mt-20">Inspector<a href="#inspector" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h3>
      <p>Two tabs. <strong>Link Checker</strong> reports references that do not resolve. <strong>Changes</strong> shows what has changed in the document, with a count in the tab label.</p>
      <h3 id="terminal" class="group scroll-mt-20">Terminal<a href="#terminal" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h3>
      <p>A real terminal in the project folder, with as many tabs as you need. Kill Process stops what is running; the tab's close button ends the session.</p>
      <p>The first terminal opens in the project folder, or in the folder shown in the Explorer when no project is open.</p>
